hadiths[69]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7354","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, and Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Maruzi, said: Muhammad bin Ghalib informed us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zayd ibn Yathigh, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, “that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent him on the day of the Greater Hajj.” With four: that no one circumambulates the House naked, and that no one enters Paradise except a Muslim soul, and that no polytheist performs Hajj after this year, and whoever There was a covenant between him and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he postponed it for a period of time. kitten
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7354 - True"
"7355","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, and Saeed bin Amir told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Muharrar ibn Abi Hurairah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: I was with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of him, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him to the people of Mecca with Bara’ah, it was said: What were you calling? He said: “We used to proclaim that no one will enter Paradise except a believing soul, and no naked person will circumambulate the Kaaba, and whoever is between him and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Upon him, peace and blessings be upon him, a covenant was made, the term of which and the duration of his covenant is four months. If the four months have passed, then God is free from The polytheists and His Messenger, and no polytheist will perform Hajj after the year.” So I was calling out until my voice became clear, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7355 - True"
"7356","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Yahya Al-Hammani Abdul-Hamid bin Abdul-Rahman told us, Al-Nadr, Abu Omar Al-Khazzaz, narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Abu Talib was treating Zamzam and the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He was one of those who transported stones. He was a boy at that time, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took his lower garment, stripped naked, and protected himself from the stone with it. Then he fainted, and it was said to Abu Talib, “Have you found your son?” He fainted. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up from his trance, Abu Talib asked him About his trance, he said: “A man wearing white clothes came to me and told me to cover yourself.” Ibn Abbas said: That was the first thing the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw. And he was spared from prophethood when it was said to him, “Cover yourself,” and his private parts were not seen since that day. Abu Tufayl
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7356 - Al-Nadr Abu Omar Al-Khazzaz is weak"
"7357","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, said: When the house was built, people were moving stones while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He moved with them, so he took the garment and put it on his shoulders, and it was called: “Do not expose your private parts.” So he threw the stone and put on his garment, “and this is a hadith.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7357 - True"
"7358","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Hisham bin Malas Al-Numayri told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari told us, and he told us Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, they said: Bahz bin Hakim told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, what of our private parts do we cover and what do we leave behind? He said: “Guard your private parts, except from your wife or whom your right hand possesses.” I said: Have you seen if some people were on top of each other? He said: “If you can If no one sees it, let him not see it.” I said: Did you see if it was empty? He said: “God is more deserving of being ashamed than him,” and he placed his hand on his genitals. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7358 - True"
"7359","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi, and Ali bin Al-Saqr Al-Sukkari told me, they said: Ibrahim bin Hamza told us. Al-Zuhri, Ibrahim bin Ali Al-Rafi’i told us, Ali bin Omar bin Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, narrated to me on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man’s private parts to a man is like a woman’s private parts to a man, and a woman’s private parts to a woman is like a woman’s private parts.” “On the man” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7359 - Al-Rafi’i said it was weak"
"7360","Ahmad bin Sulayman al-Mawsili told us, Ali bin Harb told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salem Abi al-Nadr, on the authority of Zur’ah bin Muslim bin Jarhad, On the authority of his grandfather Jarhad, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw him while his thigh was uncovered in the mosque and he was wearing a cloak, and he said: “Indeed “The thigh is from the private parts.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and the hadith of Muhammad bin Jahsh witnessed it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7360 - True"
"7361","Professor Abu Al-Walid told us, Muhammad bin Nu’aym bin Abdullah told us, Qutayba bin Saeed, and Ali bin Hajar told us, they said: Tell us Ismail bin Hafs, Al-Ala bin Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Kathir, the client of Muhammad bin Jahsh, narrated to us on the authority of Muhammad bin Jahsh, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed while I was with him by Muammar and his thighs were exposed. He said: “O Muammar, cover your thighs, for the thighs Awrah.” It was narrated on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib and Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, similar to it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7361 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7362","So Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Habib Ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Asim Ibn Damrah, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not show your thighs or Do you look at the thigh of a living person or a dead person?
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7362 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7363","So Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, Abu Yahya told us, he said: I heard Mujahid, speaking on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a man and saw his thighs exposed. So he said: “Cover your thigh, for a man’s thigh is part of his private parts.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7363 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7364","Ali bin Abdullah Al-Hakimi told me, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu Al-Ahwas, narrating on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I was cleaning the body. He said: “Do you have any money?” I said: Yes. He said: “From what money?” I said: Of all the wealth of camels, slaves, horses, and sheep. He said: “If God gives you wealth, let it be seen on you.” Then he said: “Your people’s camels produce Its ears will be cut off, so it will go to the razor and cut off its ears, and say, “This is a lake,” and tear it open, or tear its skins, and say, “This is a seram.” So do you prohibit it for yourself and your family?” He said: Yes. He said: “Then what God has given you is permissible for you. Moses, God is one, is more powerful than your helper.” I said: Oh. Messenger of God, did you see a man with whom I had an encounter, but he did not honor me and did not treat me as a partner, then he came down with me and I should reward him as he did, or should I acknowledge him? He said: “Confirm it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7364 - True"
"7365","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Aban bin Taghlib, on the authority of Al-Fudayl bin Amr Al-Fuqaimi, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah bin Qais, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him On his authority, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Indeed, God is Beautiful and loves beauty.” Al-Hakim wrote in his handwriting: “Here he brings out his beauty.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7365 - Al-Dhahabi was silent about it in his summary from this place"
"7366","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told me, Yahya bin Hakim told us, Abu Bahr Abdul Rahman bin Othman told us. Al-Bakrawi, Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that a man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: O Messenger of God, I am a man whom beauty is beloved to and I have been given as much of it as you see. I do not like for anyone to surpass me with a shoelace or a shoelace. Are we from this arrogance? He said: “No, but from arrogance is he who distorts the truth and deceives people.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"7367","So Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Quta’i told us, And Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala al-Sana’ani, they said: Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of Humaid bin Abd. The Most Gracious, he said: Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: I was not veiled - or he said: I was not withheld - about three things: about the secret conversations and about such-and-such. And so on. He said: So I went to him while Malik ibn Marara al-Rahwi was with him, and I realized from the end of his hadith that he was saying: O Messenger of God, I have been given a number of camels. You see, I do not like anyone to snare my sandals above me, who is worse than transgression? He said: “This is not a form of transgression, but transgression is one who distorts the truth - or he said: makes the truth trivial - and turns a blind eye to the people.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7367 - True"
"7368","Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Issa Al-Madani told us, Omar bin Yunus bin Al-Qasim Al-Yamami told us, Ikrimah told us Ibn Ammar Al-Ijli, Abu Zumail told me, Abdullah Ibn Al-Du’al told me, Abdullah Ibn Abbas told me, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When The Hurriyya went out and they gathered in a house, six thousand in number, so I came to Ali, may God be pleased with him, and said: O Commander of the Faithful, pray for me that I may I will go to these people and speak to them. He said: I fear for you. He said: No. He said: So I went out to them and dressed in the best of the clothes of Yemen. He said: Abu Zumail: And Abdullah bin Abbas was beautiful and vocal - Ibn Abbas said: “So I came to them while they were gathered in a house and they were saying, so I greeted On them. They said: Welcome, Ibn Abbas. What is this outfit? I said: What do you blame me for? “I saw on the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the best of clothes,” and I recited {Say: Who has forbidden the adornment of God which He has provided for His servants and good things from provision.} [Al-A’raf: 32] Then he mentioned Ibn Abbas’s famous debate with them: “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that A Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7368 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7369","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, said: Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. During one of his campaigns, he greeted a man, and a man in two torn clothes came out, wanting to drive camels, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “What? “Does he have any clothes other than these?” It was said: He had two new clothes on his blemish. He said: “Bring me his defect,” so he opened it and found two garments in it. He said to the man: “Take these two, put them on, and put away the holes in them.” So he did, and then he did. He drove camels, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked after him as if he was amazed at his stinginess with regard to himself with the two garments, and said to him: “May God strike Your neck.” Then the man turned to him and said: “For the sake of God, so he was killed on the Day of Al-Yamamah.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, as he used it as evidence in other cases. A place in Hisham bin Saad, and they did not narrate it except that the hadith is with Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him.”"
"7370","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb said: He said: Malik bin Anas told me, on the authority of Zaid Bin Aslam, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both"
"7371","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Sayyari informed us about Marw, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Qays bin Bishr al-Taghlabi, said: My father was a companion of Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, in Damascus, and there was a man from The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were among the Ansar. He was called Ibn al-Handaliyyah. He was a solitary person who rarely sat with people, but only during prayer. So when he leaves, it is only takbeer, glorification, and greeting until he comes to his family. One day, he passed by us while we were at Abu Darda’, so he greeted and said: Abu Darda: A word that will benefit us and will not harm you. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You are coming against your brothers, so do good.” Dress well and arrange your saddlebags so that you appear as if you are a mole among the people. Indeed, God does not like indecency and indecency. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out. “And Ibn Al-Hanzaliyah, whom Al-Rahwi did not name, and he is Sahl Ibn Al-Hanzaliyah, one of the ascetics of the Companions, may God be pleased with them.” ""all of them""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7371 - True"
"7372","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Saeed bin Abi Masarra told us. Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim ibn Maimun, on the authority of Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas al-Juhani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever abandons clothing while he is able to wear it in humility before God Almighty, God Almighty will call him on the Day of Resurrection above the heads of creation until He gives him a choice of garments of faith to wear whichever he wishes.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7372 - True"
"7373","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Shababah bin Siwar told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Nafi’ Ibn Jubayr Ibn Mut’im, on the authority of his father, he said: They say, “I was in a wilderness, and I rode a donkey, and held a sheep, and wore a shamla.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever does this has no trace of arrogance in him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7373 - True"
"7374","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-San’ani told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf Al-Tanisi told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muhajir told us, Al-Abbas bin Salim Al-Lakhmi told me, on the authority of Abu Salam Al-Aswad, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz reported that he narrated the hadith of my father on the authority of Thawban. Al-Ahwas, he said: He sent it to him and it was delivered by post. He said: When he had reached it, he entered and greeted him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, my leg has been broken. My boat from the mail said: Then Omar said as if in pain: We did not want to be difficult for you, Abu Salam, but I was informed of a hadith that you spoke about, on the authority of Thawban, On the authority of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the basin, so I would love for you to share it with me verbally. Abu Salam said: I heard Thawban saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The water in the basin between Aden and Oman is Balqa’, its water is harsher.” Whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, and its cups are as numerous as the stars. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never feel thirsty after it. The first people to come to him are “The poor immigrants, with disheveled heads and dirty clothes, who do not marry courteous women and whose doors are not opened.” He said: Then Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: “But I have married the favored woman, Fatima bint Abd al-Malik, and she has opened the cloak for me. It is no offense that I do not wash my head until it becomes disheveled, nor do my clothes that “He follows my body until it becomes dirty.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7374 - True"
"7375","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You must wear these white clothes, so that your living may wear them, and shroud your dead in them, for they are among the best of your clothes.” Or he said: “From the best.” “Your clothing.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They did not narrate it by Ibn Sufyan bin Uyaynah, and Ismail Ibn Ulayya sent it, on the authority of ""Job""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7375 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"7376","So Sheikh Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us, Ismail ibn Qutaibah informed, Yahya ibn Yahya informed, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You must do this.” “White for your living to wear, and for your dead to be shrouded in it.”"
"7377","So Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us, on the authority of Marwa, Musa ibn Sahl told us, Ismail ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You must wear this white to wear it.” Your living and shroud your dead in it, for it is among the best of your garments.” It was narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas and Samurah bin Jundub, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, added more words to it."
"7378","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, may God have mercy on him, Yahya bin Sulaym told us, about Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “The best of your garments is white, so clothe your living with them and shroud your dead in them, and among the best of your garments is antimony. Indeed, it shines brightly.” “Sight and makes hair grow.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “As for the hadith of Samurah ibn Jundub, I presented the dispute over it over the hadith Abi Qilaba has an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7378 - True"
"7379","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid, and Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, saying: Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, Habib bin Abi Thabit told us, on the authority of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, may God be pleased with him, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Wear white clothes, for they are purer and more pleasant, and shroud your dead in them.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7379 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7380","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman Al-Muradi, and Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, they said: Bishr told us Ibn Bakr, Al-Awza’i told us, Hassan Ibn Atiya told me, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, Jabir Ibn Abdullah told me, may God be pleased with him On the authority of them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us and saw a man with a disheveled head. He said: “Doesn’t this man have something to calm his hair with?” And he saw a man with dirty clothes and said, “Doesn’t this man have something to clean his clothes with?” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7380 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7381","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, On the authority of Al-Izar bin Harith, on the authority of Umm Al-Husayn Al-Ahmasiyah, she said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wearing a cloak that he had covered underneath. His armpit was as if I could see the muscle in his upper arm trembling, so I heard him saying: “O people, fear God, even if an Ethiopian slave is appointed over you. So listen to him and obey what he has established for you. The Book of God Almighty” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7381 - True"
"7382","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Farra informed us, Ja’far bin Aoun informed us, Saeed bin Iyas informed us. Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel, on the authority of Abu Tamimah Al-Hujaimi, on the authority of Jabir bin Sulaym Al-Hujaimi, may God be pleased with him, who said: I met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Upon him, peace be upon him, in some of the roads of Medina, wearing a garment of cotton spread around the hem. I said: Peace be upon you, O Muhammad, or O Messenger of God, and he said: “On you. Peace be upon you, greetings to the dead, peace be upon you, greetings to the dead, peace be upon you, greetings to the dead, peace be upon you, peace be upon you, peace be upon you.” That is, like this and say. He said: So I asked him about the garment, so he covered his back and took most of his leg and said: “Here, if you refuse, then here, above the ankles. “Do not say so, for God does not like every arrogant and proud person.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7382 - True"
"7383","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told me, Ahmad bin Salamah told me, Ishaq told us, Al-Muharbi told me, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, may God be pleased with him, said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of the sacrifice, wearing a red robe, so I started to look. “To Him and to the moon, for it is better in my eyes than the moon.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7383 - True"
"7384","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Alaf informed us, in Egypt, Sa`id ibn Abi Maryam informed us, he informed us Yahya bin Ayyub, Musa bin Jubayr told me, that Abbas bin Ubayd Allah bin Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib told him on the authority of Khalid bin Yazid Bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Dihya bin Khalifa Al-Kalbi, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he sent him to Heraclius, when He returned and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave him a scarf and said: “Make her waistcoat into a shirt and give your companion a scarf to cover herself with.” Then when he left, he said: “Make sure to place something underneath it so that it does not become clear.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7384 - There is an interruption"
"7385","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Yunus bin Yazid, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, “He used to feel shy for the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” “And he and his companions delivered robes for one thousand dirhams and for one thousand and two hundred dirhams.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7385 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7386","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Al-Qasim bin Dinar Al-Tahan told us, Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Saluli told us, on the authority of Amara Ibn Zazan, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, “The king of Dhu Yazan presented a gift to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a garment that had been bought.” “With thirty-three camels and a she-camel, which the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, dressed once.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7386 - True"
"7387","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas and Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “The prophets used to like to wear wool and ride sheep.” “And they ride donkeys.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7387 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7388","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Burdah bin Abu Musa, on the authority of his father, said: “We saw with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the sky struck us, and our smell was as if it was the smell of a sheep.” This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7388 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7389","Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: And while Muhammad bin Amr al-Razzaz wrote to me, in his own handwriting, he mentioned that Saad bin Nasr al-Mukhurami, He tells them, Abu Muawiya told us, Abu Salamah Muhammad bin Maysara told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, who said: “You saw us with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. I thought that our scent was the scent of the sheep, because of our clothing of wool and our food of black water and dates.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7389 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7390","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told me, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, My father told me, on the authority of Musaab bin Shaybah, on the authority of Safiya bint Shaybah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out “peace and blessings of God be upon him one morning, wearing a cloak made of black hair.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but he did not narrate it. Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: “The evidence that the cloak did not belong to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7390 - True"
"7391","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari did not tell us, Muhammad bin Salamah and Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sulami told us, they said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim, Muadh bin Hisham told me, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Kathir bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Ayyad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him. On her authority, she said: “The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was praying, and there was some sin upon him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7391 - True"
"7392","Ali bin Abdullah Al-Hakimi told us, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad bin Hibban Al-Duri told us, Al-Hasan bin Bishr told us, Ishaq told us Bin Saeed bin Amr bin Saeed Al-Qazwini, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Khalid bint Khalid, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought With clothes containing a khamis, he said to his companions: “Who do you think is more worthy of this khamis?” They remained silent, so he called Umm Khaled and dressed her for her. Then he said: “I do well, my daughter, and behave well. I do well, and behave well.” He said: And there was a red flag in it, so he came and said: “O Umm Khaled, what a sound” and “sanna” in Ethiopian means “al-Hasan.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7392 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7393","Abu Bakr bin Quraysh told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ Al-Zahrani told us, Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, Hammam, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, “She made a black wool cloak for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” So he put it on, and when he sweated, he felt the smell of wool, so he took it off and liked the pleasant smell.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7393 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7394","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told us, on the authority of Amr bin Abu Amr, a client of Al-Muttalib, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, that two men from the people of Iraq came to him and asked him about Is washing on Friday obligatory? Ibn Abbas said to them: Whoever washes himself is better and purified, and I will tell you why the washing began. The people were during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. They were in need of wearing wool and watering the palm trees on their backs. The mosque was narrow and close to the roof, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out. Peace be upon him, on Friday, on a very hot summer day, and his pulpit was short, but only a few steps. He addressed the people, and they sweated in the wool, and they revolted. Their souls were the scent of sweat and wool, to the point that they were harming one another until their souls reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was on the pulpit. He said: “O people, when this day comes, wash yourself, and let each one of you touch the best perfume or ointment he can find.” This is an authentic hadith. According to Al-Bukhari’s condition, they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7394 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7395","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Musab bin Abdullah bin Musab told us, my father told me, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdullah bin Jaafar, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wearing two garments dyed with saffron. “A robe and a turban.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7395 - Not on the condition of either of them"
"7396","Abu al-Fadl al-Hasan ibn Ya`qub ibn Yusuf al-Adl informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, al-Husayn informed us Ibn Waqid, Abdullah Ibn Buraydah told me, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving a sermon, and Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein came. They had two red shirts on them, so they started to stumble and get up. Then he came down and took them and placed them in his hands and said: “Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. Your wealth and your children are a trial. I saw these two things but I could not be patient.” Then he began his sermon, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and I did not He takes him out. And the satisfactory explanation of it is in the hadith which “
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7396 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7397","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, my father told us, and Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us: We told him: Al-Layth, Khalid bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Bilal, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, may God be pleased with them both, said: One day I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wearing two saffron garments, and the Messenger of God said to me: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “What are these two garments?” He said: Umm Abdullah dyed them for me, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I swore an oath to you when I returned to Umm Abdullah and she ordered her To light the oven for her and then throw them into it.” So I returned to her and did so. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.” The two sheikhs agreed. May God be pleased with them, from the prohibition on men wearing scarf based on the hadith of Ali, may God be pleased with him, in which the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade me, and I do not say ""Nahakum""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7397 - True"
"7398","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim told me that Khalid Ibn Ma’dan told him on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr Ibn Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw two clothes stained with stains on him and said: “These are the clothes of the infidels, so do not wear them.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7398 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7399","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Uqabi told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ishaq bin Mansur Al-Saluli told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abi Yahya Al-Qatat, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “A man passed by the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He was wearing two red garments, so he greeted him, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not respond to him. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7399 - True"
"7400","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Saeed bin Abi Orouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I do not ride the purple or “I wear a cloth coat and I do not wear a shirt lined with silk.” Al-Hasan gestured to the pocket of his shirt, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Don’t “And men’s perfume is a scent that has no color, and women’s perfume is a color that has no scent.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Our sheikhs, even if They differed regarding Al-Hasan’s hearing on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, as most of them are of the opinion that he heard from him.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7400 - True"
"7401","Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Quraysh told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr Al-Muqaddami told us, Ziyad bin Sufyan told us Abdullah Al-Bakai, Abu Imran Al-Juni told us, that Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, narrated to him, saying: “How similar people are today in “The mosque and the abundance of talīsah, except among the Jews of Khaybar.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Its meaning is the dyed talīsah. “Jewish clothing”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7401 - True"
"7402","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith and others told me about Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever believes in God And on the Last Day, they will not wear silk or gold. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7402 - True"
"7403","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, that Abu Ushanah Al-Maafiri, He told him that he heard Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him, telling that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was preventing his family from And he says: “If you love the ornaments of Paradise and its silk, then do not wear them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. """"
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7403 - They did not go out to Abu Ashanah"
"7404","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, and Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, they said: Ishaq told us Ibn Ibrahim, Muadh Ibn Hisham informed me, my father informed me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Daoud al-Sarraj, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him. The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter, and if he enters Paradise, the people of Paradise will wear it.” “And he did not wear it.” This is an authentic hadith, and this word explains the brief hadiths that whoever wears it will not enter Paradise.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7404 - True"
"7405","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Bakr told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, On the authority of Ikrimah bin Khaled, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, only forbade “The solid one if it is silk.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7405 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7406","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abu Tamailah informed, on the authority of Abdul-Mu’min. Ibn Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, who said: “There was no garment more beloved to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the shirt. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7406 - True"
"7407","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Suwayd bin Qays, said: Makhramah Al-Abdi and I brought clothing from Hijr, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us and bought from us. A man weighs trousers and weighs for wages, and he said to the weigher: “Weigh and weigh.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7407 - True"
"7408","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama told us, Saeed bin Iyas Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Saeed, may God be pleased with him, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would find a piece of clothing, he would call it a turban, a shirt, or a robe. Then he says: “O God, praise be to You, You have clothed him. I ask You for his good and the good that was done to him, and I seek refuge in You from his evil and the evil of what was done to him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7408 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7409","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Abu Marhum, on the authority of Sahl bin Muadh, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever eats food and says, Praise be to God He who fed me this and provided me with it without any power or strength on my part will have his previous sins forgiven, and whoever wears a garment and says, “Praise be to God.” It is He who has covered me with this and provided me with it without any power or strength on my part. His previous sins will be forgiven. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it. """"
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7409 - Abu Marhum is weak"
"7410","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Yahya bin informed us. Ayoub, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Zuhar, narrated to him on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Umamah, that Omar ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, called With a new shirt of his, he put it on and I do not think it reached his throat until he said: “Praise be to God who has clothed me with what I can cover my private parts and beautify myself with during my life.” Then he said: Do you know why I said this? I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, calling for new clothes and putting them on. He said: “I do not think they would have reached his throat until he said as I said.” Then He said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, there is no Muslim servant who puts on a new garment and then says as I said, and then deliberately loses one of his morals which... They clothe him, a poor, Muslim, poor person. They do not clothe him except for the sake of God, the Mighty and Majestic, unless he is in God’s neighborhood and under God’s guarantee as long as he lives on it. There is one branch of it, alive and dead.” This is a hadith that the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, did not use as evidence with its chain of transmission, and I also did not mention it in this book. An example of this is that it is a hadith that was unique to the Imam of Khorasan, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, from the imams of the people of the Levant, may God be pleased with them all. So I preferred to bring it out so that the Muslims would want to use it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7410 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7411","Abu Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abu Humaid, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih bin Usama, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Be dark “You will increase in forbearance.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"7412","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abd told me Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: I saw a man on the day of the ditch In the image of Dihya bin Khalifa Al-Kalbi, may God be pleased with him, on an animal conversing with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and wearing a turban on his head. He gave it to him, so I asked the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “That Gabriel, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded me to go out to the children of Qurayzah “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7412 - True"
"7413","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Ubayd Allah al-Narsi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Abdullah bin Omar told us, on the authority of His brother, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that a man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wearing a turban and He relaxed its edge between his shoulders, so I asked the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “I saw that it was Gabriel, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.”"
"7414","Abu Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahboubi informed us, Sa`id ibn Masoud informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, Shayban ibn Abd informed us Al-Rahman, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Kulthum Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of Usama ibn Zayd, may God be pleased with them both, who said: We entered upon the Messenger May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. We went back to him when he was sick and found him asleep. He had covered his face with the cold of the Eden. He uncovered his face and then said: “Cursed.” “By God, the Jews prohibit the fat of sheep and eat its price.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7414 - True"
"7415","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Issa bin Yazid Al-Lakhmi told us, in Tinnis, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, on the authority of Zuhayr bin Muhammad, Suhail bin Abi Saleh told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, “that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed “The woman wears men’s clothing and the man wears women’s clothing.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7415 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7416","Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Ibrahim bin Nafi’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Safiya bint Shaybah, that Aisha, may God be pleased with her, used to say, when this verse was revealed, “And let them strike With their veils over their bosoms} [An-Nur: 31] “The women took their loincloths, tore them open at the edges, and covered themselves with them.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7416 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7417","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marwa, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abu Thabit, on the authority of Wahb, the client of Abu Ahmad, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon her while she was brewing. He said: “One night, not two nights.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7417 - True"
"7418","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Mu’tamir bin Suleiman told us, he said: I heard Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’, narrating on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan, on the authority of his uncle Abdul Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, “that The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, disliked ten characteristics: yellowness meaning good manners, changing gray hair, dragging the garment, and wearing a ring with gold. Wearing amulets, performing incantations except by exorcists, striking with heels, displaying inappropriate adornments, abstaining from water in ways that are not permissible, and corruption. The boy is not his mahram “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7418 - True"
"7419","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Al-Jawab told us, Ammar bin Ruzaq told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Shimr ibn Atiyah, on the authority of Khuraym ibn Fatik, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Khuraym, had it not been for two qualities in you, you would have been The man.” He said: What are they, O Messenger of God? He said: “Letting your garment loose and letting your hair loose.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7419 - True"
"7420","Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told me in Bukhara, Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Ziyad Sablan told us, Al-Mu’affa told us Bin Imran, on the authority of Ali bin Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Muslim Al-Mala’i, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, wore a shirt, and it was above the ankles, and its sleeve was with the fingers. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7420 - Muslim Al-Mala’i is damaged"
"7421","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Abu Aqeel Yahya bin Al-Mutawakkil told us, Abu Salama bin Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both. He said: Omar wore a shirt. Then he said: “Stretch out my sleeve, my son, and stick it to the tips of my fingers, and cut off what is left over from them.” He said: So I cut off the sleeve, and it became a mouth. The sleeves are one on top of the other, so I said: If I straighten it with scissors. He said: “Leave it, my son. This is what I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do.” Ibn Umar said: “The shirt remained on my father until it was torn and it did not “We were praying until I saw some threads falling on his feet.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7421 - Abu Aqeel is weak"
"7422","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Ibrahim bin Muslim bin Rashid, the imam of the mosque in Basra, told us. Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Al-Zubayri, Khaled bin Tahman told us, on the authority of Husayn, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas and a questioner came So he asked, and Ibn Abbas said to him: Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah? He said: Yes. He said: And you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God? He said: Yes. And you pray the five days? He said: Yes. He said: And you fast Ramadan? He said: Yes. He said: As for you, boy, you have a right over us. Clothe him with a garment, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever covers a Muslim with a garment will not “It will remain in the covering of God as long as there is a thread or wire on it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not narrated by “The End of the Book of Clothes.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7422 - Khalid bin Tahman is weak"
